1
00:00:00,430 --> 00:00:01,790
Hi everyone.

2
00:00:01,790 --> 00:00:04,650
I built a system that takes a video idea,

3
00:00:04,650 --> 00:00:07,020
plans and generates the shots,

4
00:00:07,020 --> 00:00:08,086
reviews the results,

5
00:00:08,086 --> 00:00:11,290
and turns everything into a finished video.

6
00:00:11,290 --> 00:00:13,250
For this demo, I'll quickly show you

7
00:00:13,250 --> 00:00:15,940
the process and the final output.

8
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:18,720
The process starts with a simple request.

9
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:20,190
Instead of giving Conductor

10
00:00:20,190 --> 00:00:21,994
a long prompt every time,

11
00:00:21,994 --> 00:00:23,970
I moved the recurring instructions

12
00:00:23,970 --> 00:00:25,390
into the workflow.

13
00:00:25,390 --> 00:00:27,780
Now I can give it a short request,

14
00:00:27,780 --> 00:00:30,420
and the system handles the rest of the process.

15
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:33,300
The first thing the system does

16
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:36,170
is look at this existing video library.

17
00:00:36,170 --> 00:00:38,310
This library gives the system examples

18
00:00:38,310 --> 00:00:40,172
of different video styles,

19
00:00:40,172 --> 00:00:43,370
pacing, transitions, and storytelling.

20
00:00:43,370 --> 00:00:46,069
It uses those references as inspiration

21
00:00:46,069 --> 00:00:47,620
to plan a new video,

22
00:00:47,620 --> 00:00:50,170
rather than copying one directly.

23
00:00:50,170 --> 00:00:52,160
After reviewing the references,

24
00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:55,600
the system breaks the idea into individual shots.

25
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:57,650
For this video, it created four shots

26
00:00:57,650 --> 00:00:59,990
with their own purpose, timing,

27
00:00:59,990 --> 00:01:02,190
copy, and visual direction.

28
00:01:02,190 --> 00:01:04,320
Here, I'm showing three of them:

29
00:01:04,320 --> 00:01:05,510
the initial brief,

30
00:01:05,510 --> 00:01:07,020
the campaign idea,

31
00:01:07,020 --> 00:01:08,434
and how that idea expands

32
00:01:08,434 --> 00:01:11,020
into different marketing assets.

33
00:01:11,020 --> 00:01:14,064
For this project, the system chose HyperFrames

34
00:01:14,064 --> 00:01:15,210
because the video needed

35
00:01:15,210 --> 00:01:18,053
precise text, UI, and layout

36
00:01:18,053 --> 00:01:20,210
instead of generative footage.

37
00:01:20,210 --> 00:01:22,347
For other videos, it can use models

38
00:01:22,347 --> 00:01:24,030
available through Fal

39
00:01:24,030 --> 00:01:25,463
when the shot needs things like

40
00:01:25,463 --> 00:01:28,780
cinematic movement or generated footage.

41
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:30,762
The idea is to choose the method

42
00:01:30,762 --> 00:01:32,660
that best fits the shot,

43
00:01:32,660 --> 00:01:34,026
instead of using the same model

44
00:01:34,026 --> 00:01:35,640
for everything.

45
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:37,960
Once the individual shots are ready,

46
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:40,380
they're combined into the final video.

47
00:01:40,380 --> 00:01:42,183
The workflow then checks things like

48
00:01:42,183 --> 00:01:45,190
timing, transitions, audio,

49
00:01:45,190 --> 00:01:46,360
and the final output

50
00:01:46,360 --> 00:01:48,990
before considering the video complete.

51
00:01:48,990 --> 00:01:50,780
For every finished video,

52
00:01:50,780 --> 00:01:52,257
the system creates its own

53
00:01:52,257 --> 00:01:54,400
reverse-engineering document.

54
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:56,540
This records how the video was made,

55
00:01:56,540 --> 00:01:58,460
including the prompts, structure,

56
00:01:58,460 --> 00:02:00,300
methods used, revisions,

57
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:01,640
and key learnings.

58
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:03,270
The workflow also checks

59
00:02:03,270 --> 00:02:04,522
that this file exists

60
00:02:04,522 --> 00:02:07,150
before the video can be marked complete.

61
00:02:07,150 --> 00:02:08,881
And this is the final video

62
00:02:08,881 --> 00:02:10,670
produced through that workflow.

63
00:02:47,767 --> 00:02:49,749
The next phase I'm working on

64
00:02:49,749 --> 00:02:51,037
is human realism,

65
00:02:51,037 --> 00:02:53,507
especially improving natural movement,

66
00:02:53,507 --> 00:02:55,230
hands, eye direction,

67
00:02:55,230 --> 00:02:57,527
and longer scenes with people.

68
00:02:57,527 --> 00:03:00,068
I'm keeping that research separate for now

69
00:03:00,068 --> 00:03:02,607
while I continue testing and improving it.
